ncz-screensavers (0.8.13) unstable; urgency=medium

  * ncz-screensaver-idled (delegated mode) no longer asks the shell to lock at
    the saver delay. The shell is the single idle-lock owner (its lock idle
    delay is set to match dev.ncz.screensaver:hack-idle-delay), so two lock
    clients no longer start at the same instant and the lock keeps its frame
    source. Suspend locking and display power-off stay with the daemon.
  * ncz-screensavers-plugin 0.3.21: the plugin manifest is declared
    app-shipped (X-Singularity-App=dev.sinty.desktop), so the Settings page is
    populated as soon as the plugin is discovered; the plugin has its own
    Plugins category and icon, and the options of each screensaver expand in
    place under its row.
  * Launcher: the GPU class cache also records the running kernel release and
    recalibrates after a kernel change; ensure-plugin logs why it did nothing.
  * ncz-screensavers-gtk4-reference: libadwaita is optional (suggested), the
    choice lists come from the installed schema, and a build-time smoke test.
  * Regression tests for the delegated plan, the settings pane and the plugin
    packaging.

 -- Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>  Tue, 13 Oct 2026 00:00:00 -0400

ncz-screensavers (0.8.12) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Lock-hosted saver (ncz-screensaver-feed): cool-by-default operation. While
    the screen is locked the saver runs a short intro at a low, capped frame
    rate (8 fps, half resolution) and then freezes, handing the lock its last
    frame to keep. A thermal governor pauses rendering if a sensor approaches
    about 85 C and resumes when it cools.
  * The freeze is fail-closed and portable: the feed freezes only with a lock
    that understands the HOLD message. Against an older lock it keeps the low
    frame rate and the thermal governor and never sends HOLD.
  * Off-screen renderer: a GBM EGL platform fallback so the lock-hosted saver
    animates on Arm Mali proprietary drivers. Mesa still uses the surfaceless
    path unchanged.
  * ncz-screensaver-feed --print-policy prints the compiled-in policy defaults.

 -- Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>  Mon, 12 Oct 2026 12:35:00 -0400

ncz-screensavers (0.8.11) unstable; urgency=medium

  * ncz-screensaver-feed: the producer half of the lock-hosted screensaver.
    Every hack binary gains an off-screen mode that renders into an FBO
    through EGL surfaceless or a device platform, with no compositor.
  * ncz-screensaver-idled: delegated mode. When a lock renderer is configured
    the daemon no longer starts its own wlr-layer-shell saver; at the saver
    delay it asks the session to lock and the lock hosts the saver.

 -- Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>  Sun, 11 Oct 2026 20:00:00 -0400

